                <pb facs="0878" n="766" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg766"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Dawson to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-11-06"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">November 6,
                    1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Dawson states that the documents referred to in his telegram of October 28,
                    signed, and one original of each was delivered to him, and that the note from
                    the foreign office will also set forth the program, including a mixed commission
                    for all unliquidated claims, one member to be named by Nicaragua, a second by
                    the United States, and, if a third be necessary, to be chosen by the first two,
                    the department to have the right to modify this feature; also requesting loan
                    and the sending of a financial expert who should leave the united States about
                    December 15. Adds that the leaders have further signed and handed to him, as
                    witness, a personal arrangement agreeing to support in 1912 any candidate the
                    majority of themselves may agree upon.</p>
            </div>
